[00:13.44]1. Other sheep Jesus has, and they serve alongside
[00:20.16]those anointed to be Christ’s heavenly bride.
[00:28.70]All the things that are done
[00:32.20]for their comfort and aid
[00:35.70]Are things he considers that must be repaid.
[00:39.83](Chorus)
[00:43.96]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[00:54.24]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[01:02.78]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[01:10.78]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[01:19.68]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
[01:31.58]2. “Yes, you comforted me in my hunger and thirst,
[01:38.26]and whatever my need, you came to me first.”
[01:46.84]“Tell us, when did we do this?”
[01:50.18]these ones will reply.
[01:53.74]The King will then answer them, telling them why:
[01:57.92](Chorus)
[02:02.10]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[02:12.39]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[02:20.83]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[02:28.83]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[02:37.82]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”
[02:49.72]3. “You’ve been loyal to me, doing works that are fine,
[02:56.32]as you preach alongside these brothers of mine.”
[03:04.89]So the King will then say
[03:08.39]to the sheep on his right:
[03:11.89]“Inherit the earth and perfection of life.”
[03:16.94](Chorus)
[03:21.98]“If you comforted them, you comforted me.
[03:31.98]If you did it for them, you did it for me.
[03:40.89]Your labors for them were your labors for me.
[03:49.29]You did it for them; you did it for me.
[03:57.53]If you did it for them, you did it for me.”